    "output": "owner set: \"malformed pull request\" (got past the owner gate into PR-specific handling; my hand-built payload was incomplete)\nowner null: \"GitHub owner is not configured\" (rejected before any Dependabot handling)"
   },
   "evidence": "src/integrations/github.ts:85 `if (!owner) return { note: \"GitHub owner is not configured\" };` runs before every event-specific branch, including the `pull_request` Dependabot branch. The webhook prefilter at github.ts:268-269 also needs `repo.split(\"/\")[0] === factory.cfg.githubOwner`. At base, `githubOwner` always had a hardcoded login, so the null gate never fired by default. At head, src/config.ts:435 sets `githubOwner: str(owners.github, null)`, so an unset key now turns Dependabot runs off as well. But src/cli/setup.ts:100-101 warns only 'GitHub owner unset; issue-label and /limitless comment triggers disabled'. The README, GUIDE ('Before upgrading \u2026 or their issue-label and /limitless comment triggers stop', plus the config-table row) and ARCHITECTURE say the same and leave Dependabot out. The request asks the docs to warn that owner triggers stop on upgrade, and the notes under-report what stops. Doctor does still warn that the owner is unset, so the harm is limited to incomplete diagnostics."
