   },
   "evidence": "At HEAD, src/integrations/github.ts:85 returns `if (!owner) return { note: \"GitHub owner is not configured\" };` before its Dependabot handling. That guard also exists at base, but base configuration supplies `githubOwner: str(owners.github, \"MattFlower\")`; HEAD changes the default to null. The new doctor warning at setup.ts:101 and init warning at :244 mention only issue labels and comments. README.md additionally says `Dependabot pull requests receive verification runs` without identifying the newly relevant owner prerequisite; GUIDE.md and ARCHITECTURE.md likewise omit Dependabot from their disabled-trigger explanations. The defect claimed here is incomplete diagnostics and documentation, rather than the owner guard itself."
